    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0314" n="215" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg215"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.623/120: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodd</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-20T13:00:00+01:00">March 20, 1936—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 20—10:05 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>87. Your 26, March 19, 6 p.m. Verbally informed Foreign Office this morning as
                    instructed. Foreign Office repeated information to Schacht’s<anchor n="17"
                        xml:id="d149-f1"/> office and has now verbally informed Embassy of latter’s
                    approval of reply which will be returned to Foreign Office promptly and is
                    expected to reach Embassy on Monday.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dodd</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d149-f1" n="17" xml:id="d149-f1-content">
                <p>Hjalmar Schacht, German Minister for Economic Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
